You did not specify which Model Seagate 9Gb hard drive you have but if it 
a ST410899N(Single-Ended) then remove jumper J4A pins 19 & 20 if this 
drive is *NOT* the last unit on the scsi bus.

If the drive is a ST410899ND(Differential) then remove the terminators 
next to the SCSI I/O Connector if this drive is *NOT* the last unit on 
the scsi bus.

Obviously it the inverse if the drive is the last unit on the scsi-bus. 
I suggest you have your tape drive as the last device with a scsi id 
after the disk drives, ie disks 0 or 1 etc, and the tape drive scsi id of 
4 or 5.
 
EMail me if more information is required.

