>three Infoserver 1000's each with 7 CD-ROM drives attached.  The PC's
>would be running the Infoserver client software.  Two things concern us. 

You wanna walk real carefully around Infoserver's.   Protocol support
for expandability (ie, TCP/IP and others ) is nil.  If the only thing you'll
ever need them to do is that, then it shouldn't be too tough.

Frankly, if you want a simpler solution, get a PC, put WFW on it, 7 cheap
SCSI CDROM's and a cheap 1542CF (3 of 'em) in a 486 class machine or
better would work.  FTP the netbeui lanman client from ftp.microsoft.com
(doesn't take much space, and can do other things as well), and kaboom
you'd be done, and I bet for a significant $$$ savings over the
infoserver solution.

Frankly I'm unloading my Infoservers as fast as humanly possible.  They
were a great idea, but DEC dropped the ball big-time.  no OSF support,
Ultrix support was OK, but not great, really the only thing they work
well on was VMS.
