Yes,
      You can load the LATCOM.SYS file in you config.sys (or cfg000x.tpl)
file if you are using PWv5.x and then use the command 
USE COMx: MODEM_SERVICE_NAME 
to redirect port COMx to the modem pool.  You can then use it with any
terminal type software that supports the INT14 procedure.  (e.g. Kermit, 
Procomm+, ...)

Hope this helps....LATCOM.SYS is part of the Pathworks distribution

charlie



