Philip Sterne 
(sterne@dublin.llnl.gov) wrote:

: Hi Folks,

: Do TLZ04s work with 90m DAT tapes?  

: I have a vague recollection of someone saying that they can only deal
: with the 60m tapes, but somebody out there must have tried them with 90m
: tapes.

: If they do work, do you get anywhere near 2 gig on them, and do you have
: to play tricks with dump options to make it work?

: Many thanks,
: 		Phil
: -- 
: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
: Philip Sterne 				|    sterne@dublin.llnl.gov

If the TLZ04s are the 1.3 GB model (I think they are) they will work with 
the 90m cartridge but you won't get even 1.3 GB on them.  Unlike other 
forms of magnetic media, particularly 9-track, the drive doesn't sense 
BOT and EOT from physical markers (like reflective tape) on the medium 
itself; rather, the drive "counts" the distance into the tape and as soon 
as it thinks you've gone 60m, it signals EOT.  I imagine it does this by 
counting rotations of the tape spool...so...if you use a larger spool 
and/or thinner media you will use up the media faster and still hit a 
firmware-enforced EOT at the perceived EOT.

I ran into this problem using WangDAT drives, the 1.2 or 1.3 GB ones 
(whatever is correct) and got about 900-1000 MB on the tapes.  I called 
the FE and he explained what I just described above.  I assume it is 
correct since it fits my observations.  Try it for yourself but I 
wouldn't be too hopeful.

