In article <STERNE.95Jan22165118@dublin.llnl.gov>, sterne@dublin.llnl.gov 
says...
>Do TLZ04s work with 90m DAT tapes?  
>

Yes.  Try it yourself, once.

>I have a vague recollection of someone saying that they can only deal
>with the 60m tapes, but somebody out there must have tried them with 90m
>tapes.
>

DEC only _supports_ the 60m tape on a TLZ04.  Apparently the 90m tapes, 
being thinner, wrap around the tape head differently and cause unusually 
rapid wear on the head.  So after you've run some number of 90m tapes 
through it, you start to get errors.  If you're on a service contract 
they might come up with a replacement drive the first time, but if they 
suspect you're consistently running 90m tapes you'll have some 
interesting conversations with your service rep.

>If they do work, do you get anywhere near 2 gig on them, and do you have
>to play tricks with dump options to make it work?
>

We get the full 2 gig - no tricks required.  If you generally consider 
the TLZ04 as a "use it till it dies then throw it out" type of device, go 
for the 90m tapes.  If you're trying to keep it around as long as 
possible then stick to the 60m tapes.

