Huw.Davies@latrobe.edu.au Wrote:

>Can anyone fill me in on how the TK70 console load device is attached
>on a VAX 6300 (I guess it's the same for a 6200-6500 at least). In 
>looking at an old Systems and Options Catalog, there doesn't appear >to 
be a separate controller, but the TK must plug in somewhere....

Your TK70 is on a separate controller and should be connected to a T1035 
module in the BI backplane.  If under VMS you do a $SHOW DEV MUA it 
should report a dev like VAX1$MUB6 if your 6300's node name is VAX1.  
MUB6 indicates that it is in BI node 6 (slot 6, most left hand slot of 
the BI backplane) of the second BI backplane.

I hope this helps you to locate it.  Mail me if any more information is 
required.

