>Hi all!  I was wondering if anyone has information on DEC's Multia Multi 
>Client Destop workstations?  And also, can someone tell me how 
>expandable are they?  Can we use standard PC sound cards (Sound 
>Blaster), ethernet cards, graphics adapters, etc?  Is it possible to run 
>Windows 3.1 PC programs on Windows NT 3.5 DEC Alpha?  What software is 
>available?

The multia is a bound system.  The only options available are a floppy drive, 
and an external scsi port.  The systems has a fairly fast graphics controler 
(a ZLX (I think)), an NCR scsi controler (the same as on their XL series machines)
and onboard ethernet (all three connectors), and 2 PCMCIA slots.

I think there is ONE pci option slot (I haven't looked inside recently).  Though that 
option would have to be supported by NT with Alpha bits (few, if any, options).

Windows 3.1 programs run just fine, a little slower than a 486/66, but otherwise fine.
There are several native alpha windows applications, MS Office 4.2 comes to mind. 
However you don't need native alpha to run, just *286* compatibility (yes, 286).

Also, it runs Windows NT 3.5, not Windows NT 3.5 DEC Alpha.   There's nothing 
special about the NT, it comes from the same source: Microsoft.

						.dave.




