|>> I don't remember clearly the details. But, is has something to do with
|>> the order you "start" networking software. "Some" manual stated that
|>> DECNET demands having lowest, next to cluster driver, numbering on the
|>> ethernet drivers. You get the above stated problem when XWindows, UCX,
|>> LAT, or something else is started before the DECNET, and thus "hogging"
|>> the driver numbers that DECNET want. So, look through your systartup file.
|>> See that DECNET starts first, then LAT, then UCX, then others.
