|>
|>What causes this is that DECnet sets up an alternate hardware address that
|>resembles the DECnet address of the node.  That's the AA-00... address you see
|>occassionally.  If another ethernet protocol is started before DECnet, then
|>DECnet can't make this change and gets upset.  Just ensure that DECnet starts
|>first, and you won't get this error.
|>
|>-- 
|>===============================================================================
|>[                    Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory                    ]
|>===============================================================================
|>[ Mark E. Levy, N9RXF             |					      ]
|>[ BitNet:      LEVY@FNAL          |       Unix: The only computer virus       ]
|>[ Internet:    LEVY@FNAL.GOV      |             with a user interface.        ]
|>[ HEPnet/SPAN: FNAL::LEVY (VMS!)  |             (such as it is...)            ]
