    `Invalid MEDIA address' means some other system (or another network
    controller off the same local system on the `same' segment) has the
    same address.

    `Invalid PHYSICAL address' means something else has started up on
    the controller prior to DECnet, and has not indicated a willingness
    to allow the Ethernet/802.3 physical address to be changed.  (There
    are various drivers around that do allow the hardware address to be
    changed on-the-fly -- these drivers can safely be started up before
    DECnet.   The rule of thumb: start DECnet first.)

    This problem is specific to systems running DECnet phases/versions
    that are compatible with Phase IV routing/addressing -- it is possible
    to entirely avoid the hardware address situation with DECnet OSI...
 
