The DEC 3000 line uses the TURBOchannel as its I/O bus.  The models 500 and
up run this bus at 25 Mhz, and the peak bandwidth is calculated just as you
describe - 25 Mhz * 4 bytes = 100 MB/sec peak.  Actual sustained I/O bandwidth
is a function of the size of the tranfers used, but we've measured options
getting sustained bandwidths in excess of 90 MB/sec (using the maximum
block size of 512 bytes).

What the CPU pin bus looks like is pretty irrelevant to the I/O bandwidth
calculations.


