Robert Leslie (django@tanelorn.ccs.neu.edu) wrote:
: Can anyone offer advice:

: All the Alpha systems I have worked briefly with over the past few months
: have had very poor image quality on their displays. Faint ghost images can be
: seen everywhere on the screen, shifted about 0.5cm to the right of the actual
: image.

You have a termination problem!  Is there a switch on the back of the monitor
that says something like 75 <ohm symbol> / hi Z?  Try flipping this switch.
If there are two connectors for each color (red, green, blue) you may need
to get 75 Ohm terminators and plug them into the extra connectors to absorb
the signal.  What you are seeing is the video signals bouncing off the
unterminated monitor end of the video cable, bouncing back off the graphics
card and coming back to the monitor.  This is called a transmission line
reflection.  If some kind of video extension cable or video hardcopy device
has been added, it could also cause this problem.  If the above info doesn't
help, let me know what the configuration is.  I can tell you that our 3 
Alphas (and our 4 VAXstations) don't have any problems like this.


