Settings look right, but _do_ add dialup to your port characteristics.
The only remaining place to look would be the modem configuration itself.
A hayes sample might be:

STORED PROFILE 0:   B1 B16 B76 E0 L2 M1 N1 Q1 T V1 W0 X4 Y0 &A0 &C1 &D3 &G0 &K3
&Q5 &R0 &S2 &T4 &U0 &X0 S00:001 S02:128 S06:002 S07:050 S08:002 S09:006 S10:014
S11:095 S12:050 S25:005 S26:001 S36:007 S37:000 S38:020 S46:002 S48:007 S49:064
S50:192 S108:001 S109:4094 S110:002

Specifically, be interested in &C1, &D3, and &S2, E0 and Q1.

You may want to purchase a line state monitor [about $15 at radio shack if
memory serves] to *watch* the signalling between the modem and the server.

Let us know how it goes.
