: in the follow-ups I've seen, it is worth a bit of explaination.

: Short answer: OSF/1 doesn't a process name.

Correct, UNIX has only the zeroth argument to the process (it's
just an argument to the program like any other and need not bear
anyh resemblance to the program).  This is the "informational"
process name.  The shells normally just set it to the file name
of the program being executed.

