In article <1995Jan19.111933.892@batman>, system@batman.bmd.trw.com writes:
|>Does anyone know of a tool or utility that will reverse-engineer ADA code
|>and runs on VMS? They are looking for a  flow-chart type of output or
|>at least a diagram of some type to allow for analyzing existing code.

The DEC Source Code Analyzer, part of the DECset product, can do some of this
in conjunction with the DEC Ada compiler's /ANALYSIS_DATA and /DESIGN
compile command qualifiers.  Compile with these qualifiers, load the
resulting .ANA file(s) into an SCA library, and have fun with the 
REPORT INTERNALS command (produces documentation of your routines) and the
call tree browser (especially the Motif interface).
