>Does anyone know of a tool or utility that will reverse-engineer ADA code
>and runs on VMS? They are looking for a  flow-chart type of output or
>at least a diagram of some type to allow for analyzing existing code.
>If you know of one that doesn't run on a VAX, then, that might be helpful
>also, so please e-mail me.

Hi, DEC Ada and SCA both support a report mechanism that works from
the analysis data created from the Ada compiler.  You can create
reports from this (see SCA report command documentation and
the Ada /design=(comments) qualifier).  This is not really a
flow chart diagram, more of an overview report.  But it is customizable,
if you're willing to hack TPU code.

You can get get information on what calls what for several levels using
SCA's rich expression language (see SCA documentation).  Look for examples
in their documentation as the syntax isn't obvious, but is quite powerfull.

Hope this helps.

Charlie
DEC Ada


