Most of what you wanted to know has already been answered.
Here's the pin-out for the 15-pin connector.

Billy Y..

            <<< EISNER::DUA0:[NOTES$LIBRARY]HARDWARE_HELP.NOTE;1 >>>
                               -< HARDWARE_HELP >-
================================================================================
Note 571.1                        VR201A pinout                           1 of 1
EISNER::MAYHEW "Bill Mayhew"                         32 lines  30-JAN-1990 19:56
                              -< The answer is: >-
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    From the Professional 300 Series Pocket Service Guide; the Pro has
    a 15-pin connector on the back which connects, via a straight-thru
    cable, to the VR201, so...
    
    Pin 1   Blue return (N/A to VR201 -- same connector is used for
                        connecting a VR241)
    Pin 2   Green return  ( " )
    Pin 3   Red return    ( " )
    Pin 4   Mono return
    Pin 5   Ground
    Pin 6   Ground
    Pin 7   +12V DC
    Pin 8   +12V DC
    Pin 9   Blue video signal ( " )
    Pin 10  Green video signal ( " )
    Pin 11  Red video signal   ( " )
    Pin 12  Mono video signal
    Pin 13  Monitor present
    Pin 14  Keyboard Rcv Data (connects to keyboard jack on VR201)
    Pin 15  Keyboard Xmit Data ( " )
    
    As you can see, pins 4 and 12 carry the only significant "data",
    while 5,6,7 and 8 are needed to power the beast.  I believe 13 is
    connected to ground inside the VR201, which the Pro interprets as
    "there's a monitor present out there".


