The above is correct, except the 3100-38 could be ordered without the drive
plate and SCSI controller.  I had to find one reciently (DEC may be able
to find one with a 45 day lead time, but NEXL had it to be the next week).

Some clarification on the single/dual SCSI boards.  The single SCSI board on
a model 38 had two SCSI busses: one internal, and one external.  The dual
SCSI boards give you dual _external_ SCSI chains (but I am not sure about
the internal SCSI bus, but I believe that it is there as well).  So for
a model 38 we have  A & B SCSI busses and the model 48 has A, B, & C (I
think).

