> I have a MicroVAX 3100-40 with 2 1gig Hard drives, I'm running out of 
> space. Does anyone know/have any experience with adding 3rd party drives 
> into a MicroVAX, is it as straight forward as purchasing any SCSI drive, 
> setting the correct SCSI address, connecting and initializing or are 
> there any other aspects/limitations.
> 
> Oren

It is possible to just enable parity on the disk, attach it, boot, and then
INIT/ERASE it, and then MOUNT it.I don't recommend this, since you will
have any possible configuration in the NV-memory of the drive, rendering you
with a drive that times out periodically, or even worse. Your drive is not
error free since it was never low level formatted. Running a VMS on an
(low level) "unformatted" 3rd party drive is really "Glass jaw" since VMS
demands an error free device for pagefile. From my experience.

On the VAXstation 3100/38 you can do a TEST 75 to low level format a
3rd party SCSI drive. I'm mad as hell that my new 4000/90 will not!

I use the 3rd party disks that has been "TEST 75":ed in a 3100/38 on my
4000/90 and has not have the least of trouble.

See chap 7.8 in the VAXstation 3100m38 Owners Manual on TEST 75.
