Hello, fellow DEC-PRO owner!
The PRO-350 is really a PDP-11/23. It runs RSX1M/M+, RT11, BSD-UNIX, and P/OS.
Probably others too.
P/OS is a preGENed RSX11M+ for one or two users(!) and is available from DECUS.
PRO-350 use a color, or mono standard NTSC or PAL RGB monitor - Nothing fancy.
You can put in one or two RD53 68 MB HD and RX50 floppies. There is a
'verythardtofind' ethernet controller and you can run DECNET on it.
I believe the 350 is limited to max 512 KB mem, but the big brother PRO-380
can take almost 4 MB memory. The 380 is infact a PDP-11/70 derivate.
The expansion bus on the PRO - CTI-bus - is very close to being a QBUS, but
not the same connector, and not the same addressing, but seamingly the same
signals and timing. DEC also made a GPIB interface to the PRO. But DEC aren't
supporting the PRO anymore...to bad...that is the problem with the PRO.
I think the PRO is used as console to some large VAXes though. VAX782??

