> I'd like to know more about what the conflicts are.  We're trying to define
> accelerator keys for a new X/Motif application.  Accelerator keys are
> typically defined with an Alt key - but there isn't one on DEC keyboards.
> 
> Does the "Compose-Character" act like an "Alt", or Meta on a Mac???
> Any recommendations for defining accelerator keys on DEC keyboards?

        The default DECterm behaviour  with  an  LK201-style keyboard is
    that "Compose Character" acts as the Alt key.  To actually compose a
    character,  the user needs to use Compose/Space (that is, hold  down
    the Compose key and hit the Space Bar, then release both, etc.).

        I've got a newer DEC keyboard, LK401 (stolen from a VT420 in the
    machine room :-), which has  left  and right Compose Character keys,
    _and_  left  and right Alt keys, on a VS3100.  The left Compose  and
    both Alt keys, act as "Alt".  The right Compose  key  seems  "dead".
    However,  running XEV shows that each of the four keys is separately
    recognized, so one could have  at  it  with  XMODMAP to get the four
    keys mapped to their keycap labels. :-)  BTW, I can use Alt/Space or
    Left-Compose/Space to start a compose sequence.

        -Ken
