> Hi, the SET COMMAND is a very nice way to run .EXE files, how about
> the converse. Given a verb how can I find out what executable is
> being run, or the even the .CLD file that was used.

        If the verb (command) has  been  entered  in the command tables,
    e.g.,  SYS$SHARE:DCLTABLES.EXE, you can use Joe Meadows VERB utility
    to extract the VERB into a .CLD file (or to your screen), which  you
    can then examine for the image being run.

        VERB is available from most VMS  freeware sites (see the VMS FAQ
    for a list).

        BTW, you generally cannot  find  what  .CLD  was used unless the
    .CLD  was  shipped  with the software.  So you can  BACKUP/LIST  the
    savesets for a layered product and try to spot  .CLD  files,  but  I
    haven't tried that approach for the base VMS verbs (might work...).

        -Ken
