It look like the problem is with the configuration of the modem, 
not the DS700.

It is expected that the modem will drop DSR, when the line is droped.  
You can use the MONITOR PORT STATUS command to watch the state of DSR,
as seen by the DS700.  Most modems can be configured to drop or not
drop DSR.  If you consult the documentation, I suspect that you will
be able to find the appropriate AT commands.

Sometimes this sort of problem end up being a cabling problem.  If the
modem configuration isn't the problem, you might want to check that out.

