    The KA630 is the processor used in the MicroVAX II and other
    similar processors.  For whatever reason, the console ROM is
    unable to locate the secondary bootstrap.  Due to the way the
    console ROM used on the KA630 searches for a bootable device,
    it will look at both fixed and removable devices.

    Do you know if there is an operating system out on the disks?

    Getting to `2' on the KA630 countdown means control has been
    passed to the primary bootstrap -- and the error means it has
    not found anything that looks bootable.  Based on the ?54, VMB
    has likely found no bootable local tape or disk devices, has
    found an Ethernet controller, and is presumably requesting a
    downline load via the Ethernet.

    --

    <BREAK> will get you to the >>> chevrons, if the paddle
    switch on the system enclosure -- usually this switch is on
    the back of the box, and has an inscrutable label consisting
    of a pair of circles, each with a dot -- is set to allow it.
    If <BREAK> doesn't get you to the >>>, flip the switch and try
    the <BREAK> again.


