Ignoring software issues: the obvious answer is that if your problems can
be run in under 25MB (1.25GB/50), then certainly, the workstations are the
answer.  What the single large server gets you is: larger collective resources
vs smaller individual resources.  Additionally, you don't have to worry about
running the entire network, and maintaining it (one large machine is much
easier to run than 50 workstations...and much cheaper).
What the network of alphas will give you is: no single point of failure, and
much higher processor speed (on a per-node basis).



