Take a deep breath, John. Relax! DEC has lost most of its pedal digits by now,
but I think you are going a little far on these, especially the first one.

When new hardware platforms are released, they pretty much always require minor
changes to VMS. Since hardware and software releases are not synchronized and
really can't be, DEC has to issue interim releases for new platforms like the
AlphaStations.

This is made worse because of deadlines for CD pressings being quite a bit
before the CD is actually in customers hands. It's pretty much insoluble other
than holding up new products until all of this has been taken care of and this
would also not make customers very happy.

There is nothing to stop you from clustering. You will simply need to boot the
AlphaStation off of its own disk until you get the interim version for the rest
of your systems.

The auto-boot issue is debatable. I agree that it should be the other way, but
for a system aimed primarily at the PC market, I can understand DEC's choice.
Ever have to type anything on a PC after pressing the reset?

