Some suggestions:

- Turn off Autobaud on the DECserver and set the input and output speeds
to the specific baud rate you wish to speak to the modem with.  For a
14.4KB modem you can use 38.4KB, 57.6KB, and maybe 115.2K.

- Set Signal Control Enabled

- Make sure Signal Select is CTS-DSR-RTS-DTR (this is the default setting).

- Your are using the right adapter.  Make sure your cable is a 8 line 1
to 1 cable, such as the BN25G.

Modems can be painful to set up, and its not consistent between vendors.
However, with the above server settings you should be able to get the
modem to answer.  You may have to change some modem settings to get it
to hang up properly.


