  Broadcasting to local user terminals is a fully supported operation.
  For information on this, see the $BRKTHRU[W] system service.  There
  are various programs around that use this service -- the local system
  manager can install these to allow for access by non-privileged users.
  One can also use the REPLY command.

  Privileges are required for both $BRKTHRU[W] and REPLY.

  I would recommend against using undocumented and unsupported interfaces.
  (As you have recently found, these interfaces are subject to change.)

