Robert Alan Leeson, Jr. (rleeson@databank.com) wrote:
: Sorry to post such a basic problem but I'm haven't worked much with 
: DEC stuff and I have very little documentation to work with. 
: We inherited some VAXStation 4000's from another subcontractor 
: with almost no documentation.  They run but have rather small
: disks - so small we can't load our TCP software so we can plug them 
: into our net.  

: I'm tring to add a second scsi hard drive to the VAX Station---
: We have several that were pulled from some Suns as part of an 
: upgrade.

: Based on status displays the drive is being sensed but can't be
: mounted--- I think I need to do a patition and make file system
: but I can't find how to in the docs. we have on hand.  

: DEC won't talk to us because we don't have a support contract.

: Any help would be useful.  Thanks much

How about a clue as to what operating system and version you're running
on the VAXStations ? :-)

If it's OpenVMS VAX, then all you need to do is init the drive and
mount it; e.g.:

  $ INITIALIZE/SYSTEM DKA200 SUNDISK
  $ MOUNT/SYSTEM      DKA200 SUNDISK

And edit SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_V5.COM (SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM on
VMS 6.0 & later), and add the MOUNT command from above, so the disk is 
mounted on every reboot.

You can use VMS "HELP", like you would 'man' and 'apropos' on unix, to
see what the INITIALIZE & MOUNT commands' syntax and options are.

If the O/S is Ultrix, then never mind,

