What kind of disks are they?  There is some physical size restrictions on the
drive that can be placed inside the system.  Also, there are some parameters on
the drive that VMS won't like about which the Sun system may not care. 
Typically, when you try to INIT the drive, you'll get a "fatal drive error" if
the parameters aren't set like VMS likes them.

>Based on status displays the drive is being sensed but can't be
>mounted--- I think I need to do a patition and make file system
>but I can't find how to in the docs. we have on hand.  

There is no partitioning in VMS.  The drive is all one big drive, and there's
only 1 file system on it.  Do like someone else said and INIT then MOUNT the
drive.  Use the HELP command for details.

>DEC won't talk to us because we don't have a support contract.

But, they will talk to you if you want to purchase consulting.

