William Zandrew (zbytes@flowbee.interaccess.com) wrote:
: Help!  I have an inconsiderate user who thinks I have nothing better to 
: do than mess with his printer queue.

: He has a laserjet 4 that he wants to send to control through a form.  

: In particular he wants to be able to do landscape and direct the print to 
: one paper bin or the other.  If anyone has done this could the PLEASE 
: give me a few hints on where to look.  

: I have an impression that it can be done using forms, but did not see any 
: specifics in any manuals.  I don't really have time for trial and error.

I have done a similar thing (only controling fonts) using forms. The way 
to do it is set up a text library which contains the various setup 
strings for the printer, assign that library to the que, and create forms 
with the /SETUP= parameter which will call the various setup strings from 
the library.

Beware however, you might experience a multitude of blank pages between 
jobs when using this, the sollution to this is 1) use <esc>P in front of 
every HP escape sequence and <esc>\ following the PCL escape sequence.
2) Setup the que with /RESET=(RESET) and setup a reset string in you 
library.

You can find (that's where I did) this information (as well as the 
strings to be used and a procedure to create the library) in the 
Compuserve VAX forum.

Oren


