Purpose: A forum for discussions of topics of interest to -
		people involved in collecting and preserving any COMPUTER
		systems or associated communications equipment.

	 A forum for Collectors of computers whether operating in a
		Individual manner, or Public or Private organisations.


Range: 	I envisage discussions to be partly on the management of Museums
		and/or their computer/technology collections.

	The primary purpose would be in seeking information about 
		particular items, or trying to locate special items.

	One reason for a separate newsgroup is to by-pass all the 
		well-meaning suggestions of updating our systems to 'modern' 
		technology that lacks a 'soul' or heredity. (no flames).
		Even with all the www facilities I do not envisage vendors
		creating data-bases of vintage information relating to 
		mature or un-supported products.

Me:	I am Vice-President of the Australian COMPUTER MUSEUM Society Inc.
		and envisage this as an efficient way of communicating 
		with other individuals or groups with similar interests.
	I can see that a lot of our problems are to do with day-to-day
		management which must be common to all collectors be they
		Museums or individuals. The long term problems will no
		doubt be in the maintenance of working exhibits as spares
		become harder and harder to obtain.

	In the beginning I would expect interest from the Powerhouse Museum
		in Sydney, ScienceWorks in Melbourne, the Hist. Computer 
		Association of California, The Computer History Association
		(in Texas) and many Private Collectors that I have noticed
		on the net who have various vintage Digital Systems in 
		their garage or basement (bias as a DECUS member).

	The ACMS has a number of major projects envisaged for the next five
		years. These include the establishment of 'Working Computer
		Museums' around Australia; a Software/Media Archive; an 
		Oral History of Australian Computing; Library of Manuals
		and Computer Documentation and a Database of Technical and
		General Information relating to mature systems.


