Many thanks to everyone who responded: my dual-host DSSI is up and happy.

As well as all the disks having unique DSSI node numbers, the two DSSI
controllers must also have different addresses.  In retrospect, blindingly
obvious.  In my defence, it's not mentioned in any of my manuals, except
that it is probably subsumed under the bit that says "if you want to
convert to a dual-host configuration, contact your Digital Field Service
representative".  It also explains the "only six devices" limit which I
had seen but which had not caused the proverbial penny to drop.

I am especially grateful to John Hagan, who replied even before I got my
own post back, and to Bob Blunt, who actually told me how to find the
jumpers on the 3400 (KA640) CPU card (look near the things that look like
SCSI terminators ... three black jumpers = binary 111, remove W1 to get 110).

On to my MX configuration (see vmsnet.mail.mx).

